<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<dataModel xmlns="http://xmlns.oracle.com/oxp/xmlp" version="2.1"
           defaultDataSourceRef="ApplicationDB_FSCM">
  <!--
    DMT_WORKSCHEDULES_RECON_DM — Contract v1 reconciliation data model for
    WorkSchedules (design section 5, "BIP reconciliation report contract - v1").

    Re-modelled 2026-09-17 (HCM re-model: WorkSchedules -> WorkPattern +
    ScheduleAssignment). WorkSchedules is ONE DMT object whose zip carries TWO
    distinct Fusion HDL business objects, each with its own Fusion base home:
      (1) WorkPattern (the pattern DEFINITION) -> base view HTS_WORK_PATTERNS_VL
          (translated view over HTS_WORK_PATTERNS_B + _TL; WORK_PATTERN_ID is the
          base id). This is the object that has historically loaded on this pod.
      (2) ScheduleAssignment (assigning the schedule to a WORKER) -> base table
          PER_SCHEDULE_ASSIGNMENTS (SCHEDULE_ASSIGNMENT_ID is the base id;
          RESOURCE_TYPE='ASSIGN', RESOURCE_ID = the worker's assignment id).

    This report returns the BASE tier as a UNION of both proofs, each keyed by the
    SAME prefixed work-schedule/pattern name so the WorkSchedules reconciler
    (DMT_RECON_CONTRACT_PKG.FETCH_ROWS -> APPLY_CONTRACT_V1_WORKSCHEDULES) can
    match either against the TFM RECON_KEY. A WorkSchedule TFM row is promoted to
    LOADED only from a BASE / SUCCESS / FUSION_ID-not-null row here. HDL
    per-record failures arrive in the HDL response (tagged [FUSION_ERROR] by
    RECONCILE_HDL before this report runs), so ERROR rows here are optional.

    CONFIG PREREQUISITE for branch (2): a ScheduleAssignment can only succeed
    when a Work Schedule (ZMM_SR_SCHEDULES) exists that wraps the pattern and is
    referenced by ScheduleName. Verified live 2026-09-17 (--cred fin_impl):
    the four HDL objects WorkPattern / WorkPatternShift / WorkPatternBreak /
    ScheduleAssignment all exist in HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP, and
    PER_SCHEDULE_ASSIGNMENTS rows key off SCHEDULE_ID via ZMM_SR_SCHEDULE_PATTERNS
    to HTS_WORK_PATTERNS. But HDL has NO object that creates the Work Schedule
    wrapper itself (that is a UI task, "Manage Work Schedules"), and none of the
    migrated DMT patterns is wrapped in a schedule today, so branch (2) returns
    zero base rows until that config is created. Branch (1) is unaffected and
    continues to prove loaded patterns.

    RECORD_KEY = the work schedule's business key = the prefixed work
    pattern/schedule name, stamped on the WorkSchedule TFM row as RECON_KEY (the
    run prefix applied to the source WORK_SCHEDULE_NAME at transform — one key
    definition per object). Branch (1) matches on
    HTS_WORK_PATTERNS_VL.WORK_PATTERN_NAME (verified live: WORK_PATTERN_NAME LIKE
    '86348%' returns '86348 DMT Work Schedule 1', base WORK_PATTERN_ID
    300000331553350). Branch (2) matches the same name by joining
    PER_SCHEDULE_ASSIGNMENTS -> ZMM_SR_SCHEDULE_PATTERNS -> HTS_WORK_PATTERNS_VL.

    Six Contract v1 parameters; keyset pagination by RECORD_KEY (P_AFTER_KEY).
    P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID / P_IMPORT_ESS_ID do not survive into the base table for an
    HDL load, so BASE-tier matching is by the run prefix (P_PREFIX). LOAD_REQUEST_ID
    is echoed back unchanged for audit.
  -->
  <dataProperties>
    <property name="include_parameters" value="true"/>
    <property name="include_null_Element" value="true"/>
    <property name="include_rowsettag" value="false"/>
    <property name="xml_tag_case" value="upper"/>
  </dataProperties>
  <dataSets>
    <dataSet name="workschedules_recon" type="complex">
      <sql dataSourceRef="ApplicationDB_FSCM"><![CDATA[
SELECT object_type, record_key, source_type, fusion_status,
       fusion_id, error_message, load_request_id
FROM (
    SELECT object_type, record_key, source_type, fusion_status,
           fusion_id, error_message, load_request_id
    FROM (
        -- Branch (1) WorkPattern definition: positive proof in the HCM work
        -- pattern base view. One row per migrated work pattern (GROUP BY
        -- collapses translations). This is the historically-loading proof.
        SELECT 'WorkSchedules'                 AS object_type,
               v.work_pattern_name             AS record_key,
               'BASE'                          AS source_type,
               'SUCCESS'                       AS fusion_status,
               MAX(v.work_pattern_id)          AS fusion_id,
               CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))    AS error_message,
               :P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID              AS load_request_id
        FROM   hts_work_patterns_vl v
        WHERE  v.work_pattern_name LIKE :P_PREFIX || '%'
        AND    (:P_AFTER_KEY IS NULL OR v.work_pattern_name > :P_AFTER_KEY)
        GROUP BY v.work_pattern_name

        UNION ALL

        -- Branch (2) ScheduleAssignment: positive proof in the schedule
        -- assignment base table PER_SCHEDULE_ASSIGNMENTS, keyed back to the same
        -- prefixed pattern name via the schedule->pattern link so the reconciler
        -- matches it against the same TFM RECON_KEY. Returns zero rows until a
        -- Work Schedule wrapping the pattern is created (see header — config
        -- prerequisite; HDL cannot create the schedule wrapper). ResourceType
        -- 'ASSIGN' = a worker assignment.
        SELECT 'WorkSchedules'                 AS object_type,
               v.work_pattern_name             AS record_key,
               'BASE'                          AS source_type,
               'SUCCESS'                       AS fusion_status,
               MAX(sa.schedule_assignment_id)  AS fusion_id,
               CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))    AS error_message,
               :P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID              AS load_request_id
        FROM   per_schedule_assignments   sa
        JOIN   zmm_sr_schedule_patterns   sp ON sp.schedule_id = sa.schedule_id
        JOIN   hts_work_patterns_vl       v  ON v.work_pattern_id = sp.pattern_id
        WHERE  sa.resource_type = 'ASSIGN'
        AND    v.work_pattern_name LIKE :P_PREFIX || '%'
        AND    (:P_AFTER_KEY IS NULL OR v.work_pattern_name > :P_AFTER_KEY)
        GROUP BY v.work_pattern_name
    )
    ORDER BY record_key
)
WHERE ROWNUM <= :P_CHUNK_SIZE
      ]]></sql>
    </dataSet>
  </dataSets>
  <output rootName="DATA_DS" uniqueRowName="false">
    <nodeList name="data-structure">
      <dataStructure tagName="DATA_DS">
        <group name="G_1" label="G_1" source="workschedules_recon">
          <element name="OBJECT_TYPE"     value="OBJECT_TYPE"     dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="OBJECT_TYPE"/>
          <element name="RECORD_KEY"      value="RECORD_KEY"      dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="RECORD_KEY"/>
          <element name="SOURCE_TYPE"     value="SOURCE_TYPE"     dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="SOURCE_TYPE"/>
          <element name="FUSION_STATUS"   value="FUSION_STATUS"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="FUSION_STATUS"/>
          <element name="FUSION_ID"       value="FUSION_ID"       dataType="xsd:integer" tagName="FUSION_ID"/>
          <element name="ERROR_MESSAGE"   value="ERROR_MESSAGE"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="ERROR_MESSAGE"/>
          <element name="LOAD_REQUEST_ID" value="LOAD_REQUEST_ID" dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="LOAD_REQUEST_ID"/>
        </group>
      </dataStructure>
    </nodeList>
  </output>
  <eventTriggers/>
  <lexicals/>
  <parameters>
    <parameter name="P_RUN_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_RUN_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="2"
               labelID="P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_IMPORT_ESS_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="3"
               labelID="P_IMPORT_ESS_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_PREFIX" dataType="character" rowPlacement="4"
               labelID="P_PREFIX" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_CHUNK_SIZE" dataType="integer" rowPlacement="5"
               labelID="P_CHUNK_SIZE" defaultValue="5000" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_AFTER_KEY" dataType="character" rowPlacement="6"
               labelID="P_AFTER_KEY" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
  </parameters>
  <valueSets/>
  <bursting/>
</dataModel>
